{"id":"mahabharata-4-049","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":49,"title":"एकोनपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 49 · Arjuna routs Karna's brother and Karna","summary":{"en":"Having won back the cattle, Arjuna turns towards Duryodhana, and the Kaurava warriors rush to protect him. Arjuna kills Karna's brother Sangramajit and wounds Karna so badly that he leaves the field, like an elephant defeated by another.","kn":"ಗೋವುಗಳನ್ನು ಮರಳಿ ಗೆದ್ದ ಅರ್ಜುನನು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನತ್ತ ತಿರುಗುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಕೌರವವೀರರು ಅವನನ್ನು ಕಾಪಾಡಲು ಧಾವಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಕರ್ಣನ ಸಹೋದರ ಸಂಗ್ರಾಮಜಿತನನ್ನು ಕೊಂದು ಕರ್ಣನನ್ನು ತೀವ್ರವಾಗಿ ಗಾಯಗೊಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಇನ್ನೊಂದು ಆನೆಯಿಂದ ಸೋತ ಆನೆಯಂತೆ ಕರ್ಣನು ರಣಭೂಮಿ ಬಿಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"गौएँ वापस जीतकर अर्जुन दुर्योधन की ओर मुड़ते हैं, और कौरव योद्धा उसकी रक्षा के लिए दौड़ते हैं। अर्जुन कर्ण के भाई सङ्ग्रामजित को मार डालते हैं और कर्ण को इतना घायल करते हैं कि वह दूसरे हाथी से हारे हाथी की तरह रणभूमि छोड़ देता है।","te":"గోవులను తిరిగి గెలిచిన అర్జునుడు దుర్యోధనుని వైపు తిరుగుతాడు, కౌరవవీరులు అతనిని కాపాడడానికి పరుగెత్తుతారు. అర్జునుడు కర్ణుని సోదరుడు సంగ్రామజిత్తును చంపి కర్ణుని తీవ్రంగా గాయపరుస్తాడు, మరో ఏనుగు చేతిలో ఓడిన ఏనుగులా కర్ణుడు రణభూమిని విడుస్తాడు.","ta":"பசுக்களை மீட்ட அர்ஜுனன் துரியோதனனை நோக்கித் திரும்ப, கௌரவ வீரர்கள் அவனைக் காக்க விரைகிறார்கள். அர்ஜுனன் கர்ணனின் சகோதரன் ஸங்க்ராமஜித்தைக் கொன்று கர்ணனைக் கடுமையாகக் காயப்படுத்த, மற்றொரு யானையிடம் தோற்ற யானை போல் கர்ணன் களத்தை விட்டு அகல்கிறான்.","ml":"പശുക്കളെ തിരിച്ചുപിടിച്ചശേഷം അർജുനൻ ദുര്യോധനന്റെ നേരെ തിരിയുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹത്തെ സംരക്ഷിക്കാൻ കൗരവയോദ്ധാക്കൾ പാഞ്ഞടുക്കുന്നു. അർജുനൻ കർണ്ണന്റെ സഹോദരൻ സംഗ്രാമജിത്തിനെ കൊല്ലുകയും, കർണ്ണനെ മുറിവേൽപ്പിച്ച് രണഭൂമിയിൽനിന്ന് പിൻവാങ്ങാൻ നിർബന്ധിക്കുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു; മറ്റൊരു ആനയോട് തോറ്റ ആനയെപ്പോലെയാണ് അവൻ പോകുന്നത്."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.49; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"गोग्रहणपर्व","titleEn":"Gograhana Parva (The cattle raid)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स शत्रुसेनां तरसा प्रणुद्य\nगास्ता विजित्याथ धनुर्धराग्र्यः ।\nदुर्योधनायाभिमुखं प्रयातो\nभूयोऽर्जुनः प्रियमाजौ चिकीर्षन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having swiftly routed the enemy force and won back the cattle, Arjuna, best of archers, again went toward Duryodhana, wishing to do his dear task in battle."}},{"n":2,"text":"गोषु प्रयातासु जवेन मत्स्या-\nन्किरीटिनं कृतकार्यं च मत्वा ।\nदुर्योधनायाभिमुखं प्रयान्तं\nकुरुप्रवीराः सहसाभिपेतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the cattle sped off toward Matsya, the heroes of the Kurus, thinking Kiritin had finished his task, suddenly charged at him as he went toward Duryodhana."}},{"n":3,"text":"तेषामनीकानि बहूनि गाढं\nव्यूढानि दृष्ट्वा बहुलध्वजानि ।\nमत्स्यस्य पुत्रं द्विषतां निहन्ता\nवैराटिमामन्त्र्य ततोऽभ्युवाच ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing their many armies densely drawn up with countless banners, Arjuna, slayer of foes, addressed Virata's son and said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"एतेन तूर्णं प्रतिपादयेमा-\nञ्श्वेतान्हयान्काञ्चनरश्मियोक्त्रान् ।\nजवेन सर्वेण कुरु प्रयत्न-\nमासादयैतद्रथसिंहवृन्दम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Quickly bring me up to them with these white horses with golden reins and harness; make every effort with all speed and approach this herd of chariot-lions."}},{"n":5,"text":"गजो गजेनेव मया दुरात्मा\nयो योद्धुमाकाङ्क्षति सूतपुत्रः ।\nतमेव मां प्रापय राजपुत्र\nदुर्योधनापाश्रयजातदर्पम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Take me, prince, to that evil-minded charioteer's son, who longs to fight me like elephant against elephant and is proud because he relies on Duryodhana.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"स तैर्हयैर्वातजवैर्बृहद्भिः\nपुत्रो विराटस्य सुवर्णकक्ष्यैः ।\nविध्वंसयंस्तद्रथिनामनीकं\nततोऽवहत्पाण्डवमाजिमध्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"With those big, wind-swift horses with golden girths, Virata's son drove the Pandava into the midst of the battle, shattering the charioteers' ranks."}},{"n":7,"text":"तं चित्रसेनो विशिखैर्विपाठैः\nसंग्रामजिच्छत्रुसहो जयश्च ।\nप्रत्युद्ययुर्भारतमापतन्तं\nमहारथाः कर्णमभीप्समानाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chitrasena, Sangramajit, Shatrusaha and Jaya, great charioteers, with broad, sharp arrows, came to meet the Bharata as he charged, wanting to help Karna."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः स तेषां पुरुषप्रवीरः\nशरासनार्चिः शरवेगतापः ।\nव्रातान्रथानामदहत्स मन्यु-\nर्वनं यथाग्निः कुरुपुंगवानाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that foremost hero, with his bow for flame and the speed of arrows for heat, burned their groups of chariots in his anger, like a fire burning a forest, those bulls of the Kurus."}},{"n":9,"text":"तस्मिंस्तु युद्धे तुमुले प्रवृत्ते\nपार्थं विकर्णोऽतिरथं रथेन ।\nविपाठवर्षेण कुरुप्रवीरो\nभीमेन भीमानुजमाससाद ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that tumultuous battle had begun, the Kuru hero Vikarna, in a chariot with a downpour of broad arrows, attacked Bhima's younger brother, Partha, a great car-warrior."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततो विकर्णस्य धनुर्विकृष्य\nजाम्बूनदाग्र्योपचितं दृढज्यम् ।\nअपातयद्ध्वजमस्य प्रमथ्य\nछिन्नध्वजः सोऽप्यपयाज्जवेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna drew Vikarna's bow, firm-stringed and bound with the best gold, and brought down its banner; with banner cut off, Vikarna fled quickly."}},{"n":11,"text":"तं शात्रवाणां गणबाधितारं\nकर्माणि कुर्वाणममानुषाणि ।\nशत्रुंतपः कोपममृष्यमाणः\nसमर्पयत्कूर्मनखेन पार्थम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unable to bear the sight of Arjuna, the destroyer of enemy hosts, doing superhuman deeds, Shatrutapa struck him with an arrow shaped like a tortoise's nail."}},{"n":12,"text":"स तेन राज्ञातिरथेन विद्धो\nविगाहमानो ध्वजिनीं कुरूणाम् ।\nशत्रुंतपं पञ्चभिराशु विद्ध्वा\nततोऽस्य सूतं दशभिर्जघान ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by that great car-warrior, Arjuna plunged into the Kuru host, quickly pierced Shatrutapa with five arrows and killed his charioteer with ten."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततः स विद्धो भरतर्षभेण\nबाणेन गात्रावरणातिगेन ।\nगतासुराजौ निपपात भूमौ\nनगो नगाग्रादिव वातरुग्णः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, pierced by the best of the Bharatas with an arrow that went through his armor, he fell lifeless to the earth in the battle, like a tree torn by the wind from a mountaintop."}},{"n":14,"text":"रथर्षभास्ते तु रथर्षभेण\nवीरा रणे वीरतरेण भग्नाः ।\nचकम्पिरे वातवशेन काले\nप्रकम्पितानीव महावनानि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those bull-like warriors, brave in battle, were broken by one braver still, and trembled as great forests shake in a strong wind at the right season."}},{"n":15,"text":"हतास्तु पार्थेन नरप्रवीरा\nभूमौ युवानः सुषुपुः सुवेषाः ।\nवसुप्रदा वासवतुल्यवीर्याः\nपराजिता वासवजेन संख्ये ।\nसुवर्णकार्ष्णायसवर्मनद्धा\nनागा यथा हैमवताः प्रवृद्धाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The young heroes slain by Partha slept on the ground in fine dress, givers of wealth, equal to Indra in prowess, beaten in battle by Indra's son, wearing golden and black-iron armor like grown Himalayan elephants."}},{"n":16,"text":"तथा स शत्रून्समरे विनिघ्न-\nन्गाण्डीवधन्वा पुरुषप्रवीरः ।\nचचार संख्ये प्रदिशो दिशश्च\nदहन्निवाग्निर्वनमातपान्ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this way the Gandiva-bearer, foremost hero, struck down enemies in battle, ranging in all directions and quarters like a fire burning a forest at summer's end."}},{"n":17,"text":"प्रकीर्णपर्णानि यथा वसन्ते\nविशातयित्वात्यनिलो नुदन्खे ।\nतथा सपत्नान्विकिरन्किरीटी\nचचार संख्येऽतिरथो रथेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a strong wind strips and scatters fallen leaves in the sky in spring, so Kiritin, scattering his foes, moved through the battle in his chariot, a great car-warrior."}},{"n":18,"text":"शोणाश्ववाहस्य हयान्निहत्य\nवैकर्तनभ्रातुरदीनसत्त्वः ।\nएकेन संग्रामजितः शरेण\nशिरो जहाराथ किरीटमाली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of steady courage, Arjuna killed the horses of Karna's brother Sangramajit and cut off his head with a single arrow, the wearer of the crown."}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्मिन्हते भ्रातरि सूतपुत्रो\nवैकर्तनो वीर्यमथाददानः ।\nप्रगृह्य दन्ताविव नागराजो\nमहर्षभं व्याघ्र इवाभ्यधावत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When his brother was killed, Karna, son of the charioteer and of Vikartana, took up his strength and rushed at Arjuna like a tiger at a great bull, or an elephant king seizing tusks."}},{"n":20,"text":"स पाण्डवं द्वादशभिः पृषत्कै-\nर्वैकर्तनः शीघ्रमुपाजघान ।\nविव्याध गात्रेषु हयांश्च सर्वा-\nन्विराटपुत्रं च शरैर्निजघ्ने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vikartana's son quickly struck the Pandava with twelve arrows, pierced all his horses in their limbs, and hit Virata's son with arrows."}},{"n":21,"text":"स हस्तिनेवाभिहतो गजेन्द्रः\nप्रगृह्य भल्लान्निशितान्निषङ्गात् ।\nआकर्णपूर्णं च धनुर्विकृष्य\nविव्याध बाणैरथ सूतपुत्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, struck as an elephant king is struck by an elephant, took sharp spears from his quiver, drew the bow to his ear and pierced the charioteer's son with arrows."}},{"n":22,"text":"अथास्य बाहूरुशिरोललाटं\nग्रीवां रथाङ्गानि परावमर्दी ।\nस्थितस्य बाणैर्युधि निर्बिभेद\nगाण्डीवमुक्तैरशनिप्रकाशैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, destroyer of enemies, he pierced with arrows shot from the Gandiva, bright as lightning, Karna's arms, thighs, head, forehead, neck and the parts of his chariot as he stood."}},{"n":23,"text":"स पार्थमुक्तैर्विशिखैः प्रणुन्नो\nगजो गजेनेव जितस्तरस्वी ।\nविहाय संग्रामशिरः प्रयातो\nवैकर्तनः पाण्डवबाणतप्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Driven back by the arrows loosed by Partha, mighty Karna, scorched by the Pandava's arrows, was beaten like an elephant by an elephant, left the front of the battle and went away."}}]}]}